<!--
  BlockML Core — type reference value type (FQN / TypeExpression text)

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.type.TypeReference
  See docs/01_bom_core.md — Object Identity · FQN Convention
       docs/00_system.md — FQN (Fully Qualified Name)
       docs/17_type_system_bml.md — Generics · BML attribute syntax
       docs/16_framework_base_types.md — Definition Branch · StructuralDefinition
       docs/02_mbml.md — Namespace resolution · Block Definition
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <name>TypeReference</name>
  <type>type:TypeReference</type>
  <baseType>type:TypeIdentifier</baseType>
  <is>A Block type name reference</is>

  <documentation>
    ValueType for type references — fully qualified names (FQNs) and TypeExpressions that name a
    Block and must exist in the TypeRegistry. Extends TypeIdentifier (syntax) with existence and
    the branch bound B. Unqualified name TypeReference resolves to org.blockml.bml.type.TypeReference.
    Formerly FullyQualifiedName; the FQN string format is unchanged.

    FQN format (Java-style reverse-domain, dot-separated):
    • Package segments — lowercase, reverse-domain (for example org.blockml.bml.core,
      com.machineblocks.bml.type)
    • Class segment — PascalCase (for example Block, Integer, Wall)
    • Full form — &lt;package&gt;.&lt;ClassName&gt; (for example org.blockml.bml.type.Integer,
      com.machineblocks.bml.core.Block)
    Sub-Block FQNs derive as parentFqn + "." + name when omitted in source.

    Namespace prefixes in BML (core:, type:, def:, …) map to package segments; the Namespace
    Resolver stores the resolved FQN string in BOM typeFqn fields. Ill-formed syntax is rejected
    by inherited TypeIdentifier.parseValue. Unknown FQN at validate time → BML_UNKNOWN_TYPE —
    existence is not part of parseValue (doc:ValueTypeParsing). A type name that need not exist
    uses TypeIdentifier — not TypeReference.

    Generic parameter:
    • B (baseType core:Block) — Block branch constraint for the referenced type

    In type="..." attributes, write generic applications with round parentheses — not angle
    brackets (XML-safe, readable):
    • TypeReference(core:Block) → B = core.Block
    • TypeReference(core:Language) → B = core.Language

    Concrete type arguments must satisfy B's baseType constraint → BML_GENERIC_CONSTRAINT_VIOLATION.

    Any field whose declared type is TypeReference must resolve, regardless of the field name
    (type=, baseType=, abc=, …). The validator does not special-case XML sites. Identity
    `type` on BlockDefinition is declared as TypeIdentifier — that is why it is not
    existence-checked; a field named type whose type were TypeReference would be. When a type
    reference must appear as an Entity in composition or aggregation, use
    org.blockml.bml.type.TypeReferenceEntity. Unresolved → BML_UNKNOWN_TYPE: an error, not
    proof the document is ill-formed (missing library vs typo).

    Instance pointers (bml:id / FQN::id) use org.blockml.bml.type.InstanceReference — not
    TypeReference. Package strings without a class segment use org.blockml.bml.type.PackageReference
    — not TypeReference. Member definition paths (property, aggregation, association, capability)
    use the org.blockml.bml.type.MemberIdentifier branch — not TypeReference.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="doc:TypeExpressions" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Generics and TypeReference syntax.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:DefinitionModel" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Definition branch and Reference sub-block.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:TypeIdentityDerivation" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Namespace resolution and type identity.
    </see>
    <see type="def:BlockDefinition" relation="Defines">
      baseType TypeReference property (parent FQN / TypeExpression — must resolve).
    </see>
    <see type="def:PropertyDefinition" relation="SeeAlso">
      property type attribute (ValueType FQN).
    </see>
    <see type="def:GenericTypeDefinition" relation="Defines">
      parameter baseType constraint attribute.
    </see>
    <see type="type:TypeIdentifier" relation="SeeAlso">
      Parent ValueType — parseValue syntax without existence.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:ValueTypeParsing" relation="SeeAlso">
      Lexical parse vs TypeRegistry existence.
    </see>
    <see type="type:PackageReference" relation="ContrastsWith">
      Sibling ValueType for package strings — no class segment.
    </see>
    <see type="type:InstanceReference" relation="SeeAlso">
      Sibling ValueType for Block instance pointers — association types and see instance=.
    </see>
    <see type="type:MemberReference" relation="SeeAlso">
      Member definition path references — PropertyReference and siblings.
    </see>
    <see type="type:TypeReferenceEntity" relation="SeeAlso">
      Entity wrapper for TypeReference values in composition or aggregation.
    </see>
  </references>

  <genericTypes>
    <B baseType="core:Block">
      <documentation>Block branch constraint for the referenced type. Concrete arguments must
        satisfy satisfiesTypeBound(resolve(value), B).</documentation>
    </B>
  </genericTypes>
</block>
